<div class="note"><b>AI NOTE</b> &mdash; <p>PROVISIONAL machine alignment by Codex, reconciled from independent Tibetan-first and English-first proposals; this is attestation, not a dictionary definition or human approval. The medial rnam shes at Wylie 262–271 modifies its own seed; it selects consciousness at English 705–718 in the seed-relative recast. The earlier consciousness at 502–515 is an explicative grasper supplied while translating the absence of grasped objects; lexical identity alone does not justify moving the seed-clause noun there. rang gi expresses possession of the seed, but its contribution is distributed across very mental seed and the following consciousness itself clause; neither itself nor very is assigned as a secure standalone equivalent. This uncertainty is omitted, not nulled. The final de'i phyir conclusion has no remaining continuous English sentence and is also omitted, not assigned an absence null.</p><p>Binding HGM entries explicitly support 'jig rten/general belief, sngon po/color blue, dbang po lnga/five physical faculties, and rnam par rig pa lnga/five types of consciousness. las byung ba is an established glossary construction; arise from is this source's inflectional rendering, and the contained las/from and byung ba/arise members are separately licensed. ma rtogs/Not realizing is retained whole with its two tighter members. nas supplies Once. Comparative las, locative la, causal las and the second su have distinct verified ranges. All four sogs closing gestures retain their own occurrences; sogs licenses the initial and/or and requires the named supplied-head allowlist entries. Articles, supplied participants, auxiliaries, grasp/look framing and unallocated case or connective material remain unwrapped. Selection Two is original registered heading glue, with no new erratum. Textual parallel identity is not independent-publication or ingestion proof.</p></div>
